Headmaster, played by John Gielgud.

13
01:07:21,818 --> 01:07:27,818
Aces High is a 1976 war film directed by Jack Gold, starring Malcolm
McDowell, Peter Firth, Christopher Plummer and Simon Ward.

14
01:12:32,727 --> 01:12:38,727
An Anglo-French production, the film is based on
the 1928 play Journey's End by R.

15
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
Sherriff, with additional material from fighter ace
Cecil Lewis's memoir, Sagittarius Rising.

16
01:22:54,545 --> 01:23:00,545
The screenplay was written by Howard Barker.

17
01:28:05,454 --> 01:28:11,454
Aces High turns the First World War trench warfare of Journey's End into the aerial
battles fought in 1917 by the Royal Flying Corps (RFC) above the Western Front.

18
01:33:16,363 --> 01:33:22,363
The film covers a week of a squadron where the high death rate
puts an enormous strain on the surviving pilots.

19
01:38:27,272 --> 01:38:33,272
Many characters and plot lines are loosely based on those of Journey's End: the idealistic new officer who is killed at the end, and whose sister is the girlfriend of his tough but alcoholic commanding officer, the kindly middle-aged
second-in-command (known as "Uncle" by the younger officers) who is killed on a dangerous intelligence-gathering mission ordered by the top brass, and the officer whose claims of neuralgia are taken to be cowardice.

20
01:43:38,181 --> 01:43:44,181
The film explores themes of post-traumatic stress disorder (ptsd),
world war i, pilot, royal flying corps (rfc), dogfight.

21
01:48:49,090 --> 01:48:55,090
The tone is emotional.
